Auto-Submit: Yoshisato Yanagisawa <yyanagisawa@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Hiroki Nakagawa <nhiroki@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Hiroki Nakagawa <nhiroki@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1721579}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): ExecutionContext::DispatchErrorEvent on this branch already carries the is_draining_pending_exceptions_ re-entrancy guard from the earlier pick of https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8661158 (cherry-pick-d473602c676c.patch); the SanitizeScriptErrors value is threaded through that version: pending_exceptions_ becomes HeapVector<std::pair<Member<ErrorEvent>, SanitizeScriptErrors>> and the drained entries are dispatched with their stored sanitize state. SharedWorkerGlobalScope keeps this branch's DidReceiveResponseForClassicScript/DidFetchClassicScript (context only) and only ExceptionThrown gains the parameter; SharedWorkerReportingProxy::ReportException passes worker_ (a raw pointer here) instead of worker_.get(). The SanitizeWorkerErrorPropagation runtime feature is added at its alphabetical position. dedicated_worker_test.cc keeps the branch version (the upstream test additions depend on helpers this branch does not have); the web tests are carried as upstream.

